&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Lead Data Engineer to drive the design and delivery of our cloud-native healthcare data platform. You will lead the implementation of scalable data solutions built on AWS, Apache Iceberg, Lake Formation, Glue Catalog, Athena, dbt, and modern orchestration frameworks. This role combines deep hands-on engineering with technical leadership and collaboration across platform, analytics, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Data Engineering Initiatives&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead delivery of complex data engineering projects across multiple teams&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical execution from design through production deployment&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable implementation patterns Build and Optimize Data Platforms&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement batch and near-real-time pipelines&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable ingestion, transformation, validation, and publishing frameworks&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support modernization of legacy workloads Lakehouse Engineering&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Apache Iceberg implementation and optimization&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define standards for schema evolution, partitioning, compaction, and metadata management&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure efficient storage and query performance Data Quality and Reliability&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement data quality frameworks&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive observability and monitoring practices&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve operational excellence and reliability Technical Leadership&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review architecture and design proposals&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct code reviews and engineering reviews&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and establish best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across levels, providing feedback, support, and growth opportunities aligned with career progression frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Staff Engineers and Managers to define and evolve platform architecture, technical strategy, and system reliability goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical liaison between data platform engineering, analytics, and product teams—translating requirements into scalable, maintainable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ISMS roles and responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good knowledge of Information practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the manager in all the information security activities implementation and maintenance process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring the&nbsp; team and imparted with Competence related to Information security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for implementation of security policies and procedures and report any issues to the Information Security Manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–12 years of Data Engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare claims and authorization datasets.(Insurance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading enterprise-scale data initiatives Cloud Technologies&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS S3, Glue, Athena, Lake Formation&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IAM and security controls Modern Data Stack&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apache Iceberg (preferred)&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delta Lake / Hudi • dbt • Airflow or Step FunctionsProgramming&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PySpark / Spark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kafka / AWS MSK&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SageMaker&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Atlan or similar catalogs&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-tenant data platforms&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data contracts and Data Mesh concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DBT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to commute/relocate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hyderabad, Telangana: Reliably commute or planning to relocate before starting work (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process*:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with Talent Acquisition&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet with the Hiring Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral Interview(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Case Study&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview with Senior Leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Subject to change&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cohere Health:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cohere Health’s clinical intelligence platform and agentic AI-powered solutions connect health plans’ strategic goals and providers’ needs, optimizing the speed, cost, and quality of care. With an enterprise approach that streamlines payer-provider decision-making across the care continuum–including policy, prior authorization, payment accuracy, and more–the company improves collaboration and reduces burden, resulting in up to 8x ROI and 94% provider satisfaction.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the acquisition of ZignaAI, we expanded our AI-native platform with a comprehensive Payment Integrity Suite that spans data mining, clinical and coding validation, authorization and claims reconciliation, and end-to-end payment integrity services across pre- and post-pay workflows. By connecting clinical and payment insights, our transparent, AI-powered solutions help health plans proactively improve payment accuracy, reduce waste and vendor dependency, strengthen provider relationships, and build smarter, more efficient payment integrity programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cohere Health’s innovations continue to receive industry-wide recognition. We’ve been recognized on TIME’s World Top HealthTech Companies 2025 list, the 2025 Inc. 5000 list, in the Gartner® Hype Cycle™ for U.S. Healthcare Payers (2022-2025), and ranked as a Top 5 LinkedIn™ Startup for 2023 &amp; 2024.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We can’t wait to learn more about you and meet you at Cohere Health!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cohere Health is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to fostering an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all.&nbsp; To us, it’s personal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manager, Clinical Escalations to join our Clinical Process and Standards team. In this role, you will build and lead Cohere Health&#39;s Escalations Program within Clinical Operations. You’ll partner closely with Client Success, Clinical Operations, Compliance, and leadership to ensure provider and/or client escalations are resolved effectively and efficiently while protecting Cohere’s operational integrity and regulatory commitments. The ideal candidate brings strong customer service instincts, a structured approach to program development, and a customer focused presence to effectively manage sensitive escalations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the Escalations Program: Design and implement a formal escalation framework, including intake processes, triage criteria, severity classifications, tracking mechanisms, and reporting cadences — transitioning this function from the Client Success team into a dedicated program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and manage client and provider complaints: Serve as the primary point of accountability for all incoming escalations, ensuring each is categorized, assigned, and resolved according to defined workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure follow-up and resolution: Monitor all open escalations to confirm that follow-up actions are performed, completed, and documented. Hold internal teams accountable for timely closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet mandatory response times: Track and enforce compliance with all regulatory and contractual response time requirements. Proactively flag risks and implement corrective actions when TATs are at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle executive escalations with care: Manage high-sensitivity escalations involving executive-level clients or providers with discretion, professionalism, and a solutions-oriented approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate proactively within the organization: Ensure Cohere leadership is never caught off guard — provide timely, clear communication to internal leaders on escalations that carry reputational, regulatory, or relationship risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop the Escalations Analyst: Manage, coach, and support one direct report responsible for escalation tracking, data analysis, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on escalation trends and performance: Develop dashboards and regular reporting to track escalation volume, resolution rates, TAT compliance, root causes, and trends. Use data to drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally: Partner with Client Success, Clinical Operations, Compliance, Product, Clinical Content, and other teams to address systemic issues surfaced through escalations and improve the overall client and provider experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain escalation documentation: Create and maintain standard operating procedures (SOPs), escalation playbooks, and communication templates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active clinical licensure in state of residence (RN, PT/OT/SLP considered)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in utilization management operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in external client, provider, and/or member communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of healthcare regulations and accreditation (CMS, Medicaid, JCAHO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with spreadsheet functions, including data analysis and drawing quantitative conclusions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to function independently and navigate ambiguity to build a cross-functional program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills with a customer focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for improving the U.S. healthcare system and helping ensure every patient receives the best care possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ticketing or project management software (e.g., CRM, JIRA, Monday.com) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success implementing new programs is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People leadership experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing escalations in a multi-client or multi-health-plan environment is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with root cause analysis (RCA) methodologies and corrective action plan (CAP) development is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay &amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻 Fully remote opportunity with about 10% travel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🩺 Medical, dental, vision, life, disability insurance, and Employee Assistance Program&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 401K retirement plan with company match; flexible spending and health savings account&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏝️ Flex Time Off + company holidays&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👶 Up to 14 weeks of paid parental leave&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🐶 Pet insurance &nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this position is $116,000 to $125,000 annually; as part of a total benefits package which includes health insurance, 401k and bonus. In accordance with state applicable laws, Cohere is required to provide a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. Individual pay decisions are ultimately based on a number of factors, including but not limited to qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and internal alignment.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview Process*:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with Talent Acquisition for a Preliminary Phone Screening&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet your Hiring Manager!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral Interview(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Subject to change&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cohere Health:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cohere Health’s clinical intelligence platform and agentic AI-powered solutions connect health plans’ strategic goals and providers’ needs, optimizing the speed, cost, and quality of care. With an enterprise approach that streamlines payer-provider decision-making across the care continuum–including policy, prior authorization, payment accuracy, and more–the company improves collaboration and reduces burden, resulting in up to 8x ROI and 94% provider satisfaction.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the acquisition of ZignaAI, we’ve further enhanced our platform by launching our Payment Integrity Suite, anchored by Cohere Validate™, an AI-driven clinical and coding validation solution that operates in near real-time. By unifying pre-service authorization data with post-service claims validation, we’re creating a transparent healthcare ecosystem that reduces waste, improves

&lt;p&gt;The Business Analyst supports the Customer Care Exchange team as a hands-on analyst and Subject Matter Expert (SME). The role sits between Operations, Product, Automation and the Customer Care leaders. It supports IPA and GFax processes, finds and fixes process gaps, builds team knowledge through training and PKTs (Process Knowledge Tests), and uses AI and low code tools such as Claude, Slack AI, Agentforce and Microsoft Power Apps to automate workflows where it makes sense. The role also gives regular SME help to CSAs and other BAs and takes an active part in day to day customer escalations. The individual works across Product, Customer Care, Automation, Technology and GHX India&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;IPA and GFax Support &amp; Team Upskilling:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day support on IPA and GFax cases, issues and questions raised by Customer Care teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product teams to understand releases, changes and fixes, and upskill self first and then&nbsp;the wider team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Process Gap Identification &amp; Improvement:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review how work is handled to find process gaps, repeat issues and avoidable effort, and map current state and future state processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run root cause analysis (5 Whys, Fishbone, Pareto), define corrective and preventive actions, and track whether they worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give leaders clear training and enhancement inputs covering the gap, the impact and a suggested fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check processes against compliance and data privacy requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration &amp; Customer Resolution:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with product teams, other departments and CX functions to support customers and reach resolutions, acting as the link between Customer Care, Product, Automation and Technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise enhancement requests and customer issue trends with Product or IT, and follow up until closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep Customer Care teams updated on known issues, workarounds and status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;AI &amp; Workflow Automation:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Claude, Slack AI, Agentforce and Microsoft Power Apps to find manual or repetitive work and automate workflows as and when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the process side of tool changes, such as Salesforce macros, templates and automation rules, and evaluate tools to recommend the best option.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check that each automation saves time or improves quality, and improve it based on use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Automation Team Collaboration &amp; Change Delivery:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Automation team and give inputs on relevant automation projects, including use cases, requirements, exceptions and acceptance criteria, in a BRD or FRD where needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run UAT, and assess the risks, dependencies and business impact of changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create plans, timelines and milestones, run rollout communication, give regular status updates and track results after go live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;QA Audits, Process Audits &amp; PKTs:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the current BA team on QA audits and process audits, review audit rubrics and calibrate with team leaders and supervisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and implement PKTs (Process Knowledge Tests) to check how well the team understands key processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use audit and PKT results to find training needs, and track coaching actions to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;SME Support &amp; Training:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide active and regular SME assistance to CSAs and other Business Analysts on process, product and case questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run onboarding and refresher training for new joiners and existing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain SOPs, process flows, and knowledge base articles so guidance stays current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Data, Reporting &amp; Stakeholder Communication:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain KPI and quality dashboards in Power BI or Excel, set KPI baselines and targets, and track trends month to month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze cost per case, productivity, capacity and customer feedback (CSAT) trends to support business cases and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare leadership updates and executive presentations with clear recommendations, and run workshops and requirement sessions with stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Customer Escalations:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle customer escalations day to day, from first review to resolution, working with the right internal teams and keeping the customer and stakeholders updated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record the cause and learning from each escalation so it can be prevented in future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Technical &amp; Analytical Skills:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with Salesforce, including case management, reports and Knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of IPA and RPA solutions and the support processes around them, including GFax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical use of AI tools (Claude, Slack AI, Agentforce) and Microsoft Power Apps and Power Automate to automate workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel, SQL or Power BI to extract, analyze and report on data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Core Business Analyst Competencies:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a business analyst or in a similar analytical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process mapping, gap analysis and root cause analysis, with clear documentation such as BRDs, process flows and SOPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with QA audits, process audits and PKTs, and with UAT and change rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem solving and stakeholder management, with the ability to adapt to changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Communication, Training &amp; Escalation Skills:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication, able to present findings and recommendations to teams and leaders

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;General Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Supervisor owns a Customer Care Exchange support team of 15+ analysts that supports the US region on a rotating shift, and is accountable for its results. The role mixes strategic work, such as setting team goals and leading change, with hands on work, such as running daily queues, handling escalations and coaching analysts. The role uses AI tools, including Claude, Slack AI and Agentforce, to improve productivity, quality and customer experience, and leads the team through changes in process, product and technology. This position reports to the Senior Manager, Exchange Support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position requires strong ownership, sound judgment, a passion for excellent customer service, the ability to keep people motivated and aligned in a fast changing environment, and a high level of integrity and work ethic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Job Description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Goal Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team’s goals, performance and results from start to finish, including how the team is staffed and scheduled across rotating shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn department and business goals into clear targets for the team and for each analyst, and make sure everyone knows how their work supports them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the team’s KPIs: CSAT, productivity, QA, MTTR (mean time to resolve), attendance, occupancy, shrinkage, attrition and adherence to hybrid guidelines. Review them regularly, act early when results slip, and escalate when appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a high performing team through hiring input, onboarding, coaching, performance reviews and clear action plans, including support for the bottom quartile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan capacity and staffing, and raise staffing needs to management with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change Management and Team Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team through changes in process, product, tools and ways of working. Explain the reason, the impact and the plan, and check that the change has been adopted and sustained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep people motivated, engaged and aligned with team and business goals through regular one to ones, team huddles, recognition and honest feedback. Watch for early signs of low morale, resistance or burnout, and act on them with empathy and clear next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor direct reports and analysts on career growth and leadership skills, and build a pipeline of future leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI, Automation and Process Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools, including Claude, Slack AI and Agentforce, to improve the team’s productivity, quality and customer experience, and to automate routine work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize automation and process improvement opportunities, work with the Business Analyst and Automation teams, and track the results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI skills across the team by sharing good practice and use cases, and by coaching analysts to use the tools well and to protect customer data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively create projects and process efficiencies that improve scalability, quality and customer satisfaction, and keep process documents and resource materials current so the whole team works to one standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customers, Escalations and Cross Functional Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support customers and GHX coworkers by phone and email, and own escalations and related product issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Automation, Technology and other CX teams to resolve problems and to raise customer issues and trends early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give analysts clear and actionable instructions for daily tasks and project work, and manage own time, projects and meetings to deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear updates for leaders on team performance, risks, progress on change and the results of AI and automation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Required Skills/Competencies&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and accountability for team results, with the integrity to follow through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead change: explain the reason, bring people along, handle resistance and make new ways of working stick.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to motivate people, build trust and keep a team aligned with team and business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinking: connect daily work to business goals, set priorities and decide using data, while staying hands on where the team needs it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical use of AI tools such as Claude, Slack AI and Agentforce, with good judgment on data privacy and the quality of AI output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to monitor and evaluate performance using KPIs such as CSAT, productivity, QA, MTTR, attendance, occupancy, shrinkage, attrition and hybrid guidelines, and to turn the numbers into action, including bottom quartile management and employee satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coaching and feedback skills, including handling difficult conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and effective verbal and written communication, including presenting to GHX leaders and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office, with advanced Excel, and working knowledge of Salesforce or a similar CRM tool.&lt;/li&gt;
