&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced DevOps Team Lead to lead our DevOps engineering team in building, scaling, and securing the infrastructure that powers Cohere Health&#39;s platform. In this role you will drive technical direction, mentor engineers, own cross-functional delivery, and partner closely with engineering, security, and data teams to ensure our infrastructure is reliable, secure, and scalable in a regulated healthcare environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a technical leadership role for someone who is equally comfortable reviewing a Terraform module, running a sprint planning session, and presenting infrastructure strategy to engineering leadership. You will be expected to lead from the front — not just delegate, but contribute directly alongside your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-first role that may require travel to Boston, MA for new hire onboarding and occasional in-person team meetings and company events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a team of DevOps engineers — setting technical direction, running sprint planning, and driving delivery against quarterly goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, deploy, and maintain highly scalable, secure production infrastructure on AWS using infrastructure-as-code practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve CI/CD pipelines — establishing consistent deployment standards and security gates across engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migrations from legacy infrastructure to modern, managed platforms and decommission outdated systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive our observability strategy — building out monitoring, logging, alerting, and on-call routing across all services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own networking and access management — ensuring secure, well-documented, least-privilege access across all environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed security into the DevOps lifecycle — vulnerability scanning, code and infrastructure analysis, and remediation workflows with clear SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a FinOps practice — driving cloud cost optimization, right-sizing workloads, and reporting spend to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary escalation point for infrastructure incidents and lead postmortems with preventive follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure infrastructure meets healthcare regulatory and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years working in DevOps, SRE, or infrastructure engineering, with experience mentoring or leading other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience building and managing cloud infrastructure at scale — compute, networking, storage, identity, and access management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building and maintaining automated build, test, and deployment pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security practices and compliance frameworks, including vulnerability scanning, cloud security posture management, and audit logging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up and managing monitoring, logging, and alerting systems to maintain production reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable writing code in at least one scripting or systems language, and managing infrastructure through code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can shift between deep technical work, team leadership, and translating infrastructure decisions for non-technical partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience in a regulated industry (especially healthcare), container orchestration, AI-driven automation for infrastructure, or cloud platform certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
