&lt;li&gt;Translates strategic and operational workflows into clear business and functional requirements, partnering with Salesforce engineering to deliver solutions that meet the needs of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns a clean, well-documented sales funnel model — pipeline stages, opportunity fields, account hierarchies — and maps data across systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads AI strategy within the Salesforce ecosystem, identifying and building automation that reduces manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoots system issues quickly and is the first point of escalation for sales tooling problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality &amp; Process Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; The Director is the steward of data quality and process discipline across our GTM systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Runs regular data hygiene audits — duplicate records, stale opportunities, missing fields — and drives resolution with sales teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns QA through the deal lifecycle, from S1 opportunities to go-live — validating products, pricing, and contract terms against Salesforce before a deal is handed off to implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defines, governs, and maintains the business rules for Maven&#39;s customer account hierarchy, including new accounts, restructures, and ongoing hygiene, to support accurate reporting and client operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documents and enforces sales process standards (stage definitions, required fields, deal desk workflows) so the pipeline reflects reality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Operations Support:&lt;/strong&gt; The Director is a hands-on operator across the broader GTM and Finance functions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with Sales, Finance, Customer Success, and Engineering to identify bottlenecks and convert them into system-level solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives business analysis and program management for Salesforce-related initiatives, including scoping new requests, running discovery, and managing multi-phase implementation roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports Deal Desk with opportunity structuring, approval workflows, new pricing, and contract data accuracy in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years across Salesforce architecture, revenue operations, or GTM systems, including time at a B2B SaaS or healthcare company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on Salesforce skill: Understands best-practice system architecture and can design clear business and system requirements to achieve that build. Has designed account hierarchies and object models for complex B2B organizations, ideally where revenue moves through more than one channel or contract structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built their own automation and AI-enabled tooling to replace manual GTM and revenue operations work; continually identifies inefficient processes and eliminates them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has integrated Salesforce with the systems around it — data warehouse, BI, billing, and GTM tooling. At Maven this means Looker, BigQuery, NetSuite, Gong, ZoomInfo, and Clay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Looker or equivalent BI, with a track

