&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Senior Forward-Deployed Engineer to join our Forward Deployed Engineering team at Cohere Health. In this highly technical, customer-facing role, you will own end-to-end technical integration work with enterprise customers and partners—from pre-sales through production deployment—bridging complex healthcare systems with Cohere’s AI-first platform. You’ll partner closely with Engineering, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Customer Success teams to design and execute sophisticated integrations that improve access to care for millions of members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end technical integration design and execution for enterprise customers, from initial scoping through production deployment, serving as the primary technical authority throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical discovery, scoping, and proof-of-concept work during pre-sales cycles, creating technical proposals and estimates to validate feasibility for prospective customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design system architectures that bridge customer IT environments with Cohere’s platform, making key architectural decisions that balance customer constraints with platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with AI/ML-enabled healthcare features—including clinical decision support, automated review, and intelligent routing—ensuring they meet regulatory requirements and clinical safety standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-quality technical artifacts including integration designs, architecture diagrams, data mappings, API implementation guides, and operational runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable integration patterns and templates that scale across customers, and continuously identify opportunities to improve platform capabilities based on implementation learnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Engineering, Product, Solutions Architecture, and Customer Success teams to drive successful go-live outcomes and mentor junior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10+ years of software engineering experience with a strong backend/systems focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in relevant field is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare industry experience, particularly on the payer side (health plans, managed care organizations), including familiarity with healthcare workflows, data standards, and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in data architecture and integration patterns: data modeling, transformation logic, schema design, and enterprise integration patterns (middleware, message queues, event-driven architectures)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AWS cloud platforms (Lambda, ECS, RDS, S3, API Gateway, EventBridge)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong API integration and authentication experience: RESTful APIs, webhooks, OAuth2/OIDC, SAML 2.0, JWT, mTLS, and API key management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production coding skills in modern languages (Python, Node.js, Java, Go, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with enterprise customers in technical implementation roles (not just internal teams)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and high agency: ability to define problems, propose solutions, and execute independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with payer-side technology: prior authorization platforms, utilization management systems, or claims processing is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with healthcare data standards: FHIR, X12 (837, 278, 275), HL7v2, or similar specifications is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI/ML integration experience: working with LLMs, embedding AI capabilities into production systems, or ML model deployment is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure-as-code experience with Terraform, CloudFormation, or similar tools is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated environments (HIPAA, SOC2, HITRUST) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Database expertise: SQL and NoSQL (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, DynamoDB), query optimization, and data modeling is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity and access management (IAM) experience: SSO implementations, federated identity, RBAC, and multi-tenancy security patterns is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
