&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a&nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Clinical Informatician&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;to serve as a key bridge between clinical expertise and data science. In this advanced role, you’ll apply deep clinical reasoning and informatics expertise to design, evaluate, and optimize data-driven healthcare solutions. You’ll also lead ontology mapping, structured data validation, and annotation quality initiatives supporting our next-generation AI and LLM-enabled healthcare tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote-first role that may require travel to Boston, MA for new hire onboarding and occasional in-person team meetings and company events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with clinicians, data scientists, and engineers to design and validate digital health and analytics solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate clinical workflows into structured data and logic for algorithms and quality measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts in ontology mapping, terminology management (SNOMED, ICD, LOINC, RxNorm), and interoperability standards (FHIR, HL7).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee labeling and abstraction to ensure model safety, accuracy, and clinical integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior informaticians and specialists in annotation, data validation, and workflow improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSN or related clinical degree with active RN license required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6+ years of experience in clinical informatics, analytics, or digital health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced understanding of clinical data, EHR systems, and data standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data modeling or AI-driven healthcare products preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s degree or informatics certification (RN-BC, CPHIMS, ACHIP, etc.) a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay &amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💻 Fully remote opportunity with about 5% travel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🩺 Medical, dental, vision, life, disability insurance, and Employee Assistance Program&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 401K retirement plan with company match; flexible spending and health savings account&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏝️ Up to 184 hours (23 days) of PTO per year + company holidays&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👶 Up to 14 weeks of paid parental leave&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🐶 Pet insurance &nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The salary range for this position is $85,000.00 to $100,000.00 annually; as part of a total benefits package which includes health insurance, 401k and bonus. In accordance with state applicable laws, Cohere is required to provide a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. Individual pay decisions are ultimately based on a number of factors, including but not limited to qualifications for the role, experience level, skillset, and internal alignment.&lt;/p&gt;
