&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity Overview:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Software Engineer I to join our Integrations team. In this role, you will be designing, developing, testing, and supporting healthcare integration systems that connect Cohere Health with providers, payers, delegated entities, and third-party platforms. You&#39;ll work as part of a fast-paced, autonomous, agile team of software engineers building and operating a growing enterprise integration platform. This is an opportunity to develop your technical expertise at the intersection of healthcare interoperability, APIs, and modern distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, develop, test, and maintain reliable and scalable services that support critical business workflows and enterprise integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration Solutions:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain secure integrations with internal and external platforms, partners, and third-party systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and support APIs and work with external APIs, data exchange protocols, and common integration patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Work with event-driven architectures, asynchronous messaging, and distributed systems to support reliable and scalable processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud &amp; Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to cloud infrastructure, CI/CD pipelines, deployment automation, and software delivery practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop automated unit, integration, and end-to-end tests and contribute to improving the team&#39;s testing frameworks and practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Use monitoring, logging, metrics, and observability tools to troubleshoot issues and improve system reliability and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Troubleshoot and resolve integration and production issues and participate in on-call and operational support activities as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security:&lt;/strong&gt; Implement secure integrations using authentication, authorization, access control, and API security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with product, operations, QA, infrastructure, and other engineering teams to deliver integration solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in technical discussions, planning, backlog refinement, code reviews, and delivery activities within an agile development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp; Knowledge Sharing:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to technical documentation and share knowledge and best practices across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to improve code quality, system reliability, engineering processes, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering or related field; or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of experience in software development building and supporting applications or services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with at least one modern programming language such as Java, Python, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with REST APIs, HTTP, JSON, and common integration patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing unit and/or integration tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relational and/or non-relational databases and data modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of software development practices, version control, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with engineers and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of authentication, authorization, and secure API design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and supporting integrations with external APIs or third-party systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event-driven architecture, asynchronous messaging, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated integration or end-to-end testing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud platforms, Infrastructure as Code, or CI/CD pipeline design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability, monitoring, logging, and production troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare technology, health plan operations, or prior authorization systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with healthcare interoperability standards such as FHIR or other healthcare data exchange protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
