&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The IT Systems Engineer is responsible for administering, supporting, and continuously improving eClinical Solutions’ enterprise technology platforms and related infrastructure. The position also supports the company’s core technology infrastructure, including servers, networks, switches, routers, wireless access points, firewalls, backup and recovery systems, and hosted services. Responsibilities include platform configuration, identity and access management, endpoint management, application integration, automation, monitoring, troubleshooting, documentation, and operational support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The IT Systems Engineer works across functional and technical areas and may assume additional responsibilities based on evolving business, security, compliance, and operational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY TASKS &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and support Microsoft 365, including Entra ID, Intune, Windows Autopilot, SharePoint Online, Teams, Exchange, Azure, and other services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and support Atlassian platforms, including Jira, Jira Service Management (JSM), Assets, Confluence and other services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain platform workflows, forms, permissions, roles, groups, integrations, automation rules, and reporting capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage identity and access controls, endpoint configuration, application deployment, device compliance, and user lifecycle processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support enterprise application integrations using APIs, connectors, scripting, and automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and support network and infrastructure technologies, including servers, switches, routers, wireless access points, firewalls, DNS, DHCP, SFTP, and related services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor enterprise platforms and infrastructure for availability, capacity, performance, security, and operational issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage or support backup, recovery, disaster-recovery, and business-continuity technologies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex platform, endpoint, identity, integration, network, and infrastructure issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident, problem, change, vulnerability, compliance, and audit-management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain technical documentation, configuration standards, operating procedures, recovery documentation, and knowledge articles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and recommend improvements to enterprise platforms, infrastructure, security controls, automation, and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with IT Support, Information Security, Engineering, Application Operations, business stakeholders, and third-party providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in information technology, computer science, or equivalent combination of education, professional training, certifications, and relevant work experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five or more years of experience administering and supporting enterprise technology platforms, systems, networks, or related infrastructure, preferably within a SaaS technology company or regulated environment preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting distributed users and technology services across multiple offices, regions, or time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certifications from Microsoft, Atlassian, AWS, Cisco, CompTIA, or similar providers are preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal English communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, troubleshooting, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take ownership of technical issues, coordinate the appropriate resources, and drive work through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to balance operational support, planned initiatives, and changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate business and operational requirements into practical technical configurations and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to both technical and nontechnical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and maintain clear technical documentation, operating procedures, system records, and knowledge articles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail when administering permissions, configurations, integrations, and production technology services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with IT Support, Information Security, Engineering, Application Operations, business stakeholders, and external service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment when evaluating operational risk, security requirements, user impact, and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability and willingness to learn, administer, and support new technologies as business needs evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to customer service, operational reliability, continuous improvement, and timely follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to participate effectively in incident response, change management, projects, audits, and cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong administration and troubleshooting experience within the Microsoft 365 ecosystem, including Entra ID, Intune, Windows Autopilot, Exchange Online, SharePoint Online, Teams, and related Azure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Atlassian platforms such as Jira, Jira Service Management, Assets, and Confluence, including workflows, permissions, request types, forms, automation, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of identity and access management, including Active Directory, Entra ID, role-based access control, user and group administration, single sign-on, multifactor authentication, and user lifecycle processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing endpoint configuration, compliance policies, application deployment, device enrollment, operating-system updates, and security settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of enterprise networking and infrastructure technologies, including switches, routers, firewalls, wireless access points, virtual servers, DNS, DHCP, VPN, and SFTP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting backup and recovery technologies, system monitoring, disaster-recovery processes, and business-continuity testing.

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sales Systems Analyst (Salesforce Administrator) will be responsible for the day-to-day administration, configuration, development and ongoing optimization of the company&#39;s Salesforce.com environment, ensuring it is a reliable, scalable and accurate system of record for the global sales organization. This role will also support integrations with related sales technologies and will build and maintain the reports and dashboards used for weekly, monthly and quarterly sales reporting. Working closely with Global Sales Operations, Finance, IT and business stakeholders, this role will play a critical part in turning business requirements into practical Salesforce solutions that improve sales productivity, data integrity and forecasting predictability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY TASKS &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salesforce Administration &amp; Support:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily administration of Salesforce.com, including user setup and deactivation, roles, profiles, permission sets, sharing rules and license management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for Salesforce support requests, triaging, prioritizing and resolving issues in a timely manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage sandboxes, seasonal Salesforce releases and change control, testing new functionality and communicating impacts to users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain system documentation, including data dictionaries, configuration details and process flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Configuration &amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build and maintain solutions, including custom objects and fields, page layouts, validation rules, lightning pages and flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and translate business requirements into technical specifications and deliver solutions through a documented build, test and deployment process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and prioritize enhancement requests with Global Sales Operations and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrations &amp; Data Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and enhance integrations between Salesforce and other sales technologies and, as needed, assist with administration of those tools, working with IT and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations using native connectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure data integrity and accuracy within the CRM through data quality rules, duplicate management, routine audits and clean-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage data imports, exports, migrations and mass updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp; Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, update and maintain reports and dashboards that support weekly, monthly and quarterly sales reporting, pipeline visibility and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to ad hoc reporting and data requests from sales leadership and cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor system usage and adoption metrics and recommend improvements to maximize the return on sales technology investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvement &amp; User Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global Sales Operations to identify opportunities to streamline sales processes and automate manual work within Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop user guides and release notes, and deliver training to help the sales team make effective use of Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with marketing, proposals and solution consulting teams to align Salesforce processes and data across the go-to-market lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other duties as assigned, including additional sales systems projects and responsibilities as the function evolves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Business Administration, or a related field and/or equivalent work experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience administering and configuring Salesforce.com preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a life sciences or other regulated industry preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Certified Administrator required; Salesforce Platform App Builder and/or Platform Developer I preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills, with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple and shifting priorities, adapt to evolving processes and work independently in a fast-paced, global environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative approach, with a service mindset toward internal customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Salesforce.com configuration, including security model, Flows, validation rules, reports and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Apex, SOQL, Lightning Web Components and Salesforce APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Salesforce with other tools such as Gong and HubSpot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data management tools such as Data Loader, and with deployment tools such as change sets, Salesforce CLI or DevOps platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite, particularly Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Use Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees are expected to appropriately leverage company-approved AI tools to improve productivity and quality while adhering to company policies, protecting confidential information, validating AI-generated content, and exercising sound professional judgment. AI is intended to augment—not replace—professional judgment, critical thinking, accountability, and decision-making.&nbsp;Accountability for all work remains with the employee.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OVERVIEW&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager, Service Management &amp; Automation owns the IT service management practice and the automation and agent estate for Enterprise Technology &amp; Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role has three parts. The first is practice: owning incident, problem, service request, change and continual improvement as governed ITIL practices, together with the classification standard and data quality that make them measurable. The second is performance: aggregating and reporting service results across all four ET&amp;O functions and running the monthly and quarterly review cadence. The third is automation: owning the backlog of work to be automated, the agents and robotic processes that perform it, and the controls that keep them inside the bounds set by the AI Governance Council.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role is deliberately distinct from Global Service Operations and is designed to complement it. Global Service Operations runs the service: the shift roster, the tiers, the people and day-to-day resolution. This role owns the practice those teams work to, the platform they work in, the data that evidences what happened, and the automation that removes the work. Where the two meet — tier definitions, service level targets, the automation backlog — the standard is set here and delivered there. The same relationship applies to Infrastructure &amp; Platforms and Business Applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a peer-level function lead reporting to the Vice President, Information Technology and Head of Enterprise Technology &amp; Operations, based in the eCS India office and supporting eClinical Solutions employees globally. It is accountable for the service management platform — currently Zendesk, migrating to Atlassian Jira Service Management — and works within eClinical Solutions quality standards, including GxP and 21 CFR Part 11 obligations where they apply to IT systems and records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY TASKS &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ITSM Practice Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the IT service management practice across incident, problem, service request, change and continual improvement, including practice definition, adherence and audit. Delivery against those practices sits with the respective function leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the service catalogue, request taxonomy and classification standard across all four ET&amp;O functions, and hold classification completeness at 100% on ticket closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the service level framework and the L1, L2 and L3 tier definitions with the function leads; Global Service Operations owns the roster and the operational escalation path within it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own problem management end to end: chair the problem review, drive root cause to closure with the owning function, and track repeat causes out of the estate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the practice documentation set — process definitions, work instructions and the knowledge standard — to audit quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Performance Reporting &amp; Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aggregate and report overall service performance across all four ET&amp;O functions — Global Service Operations, Infrastructure &amp; Platforms, Service Management &amp; Automation, and&nbsp;Business Applications — into a single view for the Head of ET&amp;O and the Chief Transformation &amp; AI Officer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with each functional lead to define, baseline, measure, report and improve the KPIs and metrics for their area, holding the definitions consistent so that results are comparable across functions and over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the monthly service review: attainment against service levels, backlog age and composition, automation coverage, agent-caused incidents, and actions carried forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the quarterly business review: trend across the quarter, progress against the 2027 objectives and MBOs, total cost of ownership for AI and automation, and the forward plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce the evidence pack for internal and client audits and for customer qualification activity, drawn from the service record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Service Management Platform &amp; Data&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as product owner for the ITSM platform, including the migration from Zendesk to Atlassian Jira Service Management and ownership of the configuration baseline thereafter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the classification standard is agreed and enforced before platform cutover, so that the standard is migrated rather than the current data quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and run the configuration management database and asset data model to the standard required by automated routing, impact analysis and audit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the data quality of the service record — priority, tier, resolution type, subcategory and resolution group — and the controls that keep it populated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace unstructured email intake with structured catalogue items and guided forms, working with the functions that receive the demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the ITSM platform vendor relationship, licensing and roadmap alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp; Agent Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the enterprise automation backlog for ET&amp;O: identify, size, prioritise and sequence candidates by volume, effort and business impact, drawing candidates from every function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the automation standards, patterns and review gates that all build teams work to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Business Application Support team to drive service improvement and automation delivery, chairing the joint backlog review and directing demand to their build capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Center of AI and Automation (CoA+) to design, build and deploy the AI and RPA solutions identified in the automation backlog, in line with the agreed MBOs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operate the agent lifecycle, covering:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proposal, validation, deployment, monitoring and retirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A named human owner and a retirement path for every production agent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence thresholds, exception handling and hand-back paths between agents and humans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the agent registry and the autonomy bounds recorded by the AI Governance Council, within CORPPOL-13 and the Acceptable Use Addendum.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend agent lifecycle governance to the existing robotic process automation estate, which today operates without a backlog, release discipline or defined ownership.&lt;/li&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maven Clinic is the world&#39;s largest virtual clinic for women and families on a mission to make healthcare work for all of us. Through Maven Enterprise, the company partners with more than 2,300 employers and health plans to provide end-to-end women&#39;s and family health programs spanning fertility and family building, maternity and newborn care, parenting and pediatrics, and menopause and midlife — improving clinical outcomes, reducing healthcare costs, and expanding equitable access to high-quality care at scale. Through its consumer platform, Maven provides direct access to virtual care across 30+ specialties, as well as dedicated hormone and GLP-1 care programs purpose-built for women. Founded in 2014 by CEO Kate Ryder, Maven Clinic has raised more than $425 million from leading healthcare and technology investors including General Catalyst, Sequoia, Dragoneer Investment Group, Oak HC/FT, StepStone Group, Icon Ventures, and Lux Capital. Recognized for innovation and industry leadership, Maven has been named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies, CNBC Disruptor 50, Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative Companies, and FORTUNE Best Places to Work. Learn more at mavenclinic.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An award-winning culture working towards an important mission –&nbsp; Maven Clinic is a recipient of over 30 workplace and innovation awards, including:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TIME 100 Most Influential Companies (2023, 2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Change the World (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC Disruptor 50 List (2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an experienced Contract Senior Recruiter for a 6-month contract to support full-cycle recruiting across multiple business functions, with a focus on high-velocity, non-technical hiring. You’ll partner closely with hiring managers to move searches forward efficiently, build strong talent pipelines, and deliver a great candidate experience. You’ll also take on more complex searches as needed, using hands-on, creative sourcing strategies to find talent in competitive or hard-to-reach markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full-cycle recruiting across functions such as Finance, Growth, Sales, and G&amp;A managing multiple searches simultaneously in a fast-paced, high-velocity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers to understand business needs, align on role requirements, and develop effective recruiting strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute sourcing strategies to attract qualified candidates efficiently, while conducting deeper, targeted sourcing for specialized or hard-to-fill roles as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage candidate pipelines, screening, interviews, feedback, and offer processes to keep searches moving and hiring teams aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver an exceptional candidate experience through timely communication, thoughtful engagement, and a smooth, transparent hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise hiring managers on talent availability, market trends, and sourcing approaches to support effective hiring decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate ATS data and pipeline visibility to track progress and support hiring goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of in-house, full-cycle recruiting experience across non-technical business functions, such as Finance, Sales, Growth, G&amp;A, or similar areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a high volume of requisitions and move quickly without compromising candidate quality or experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on sourcing skills, with the ability to independently identify, engage, and build pipelines of qualified candidates using creative sourcing strategies and a variety of tools and channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with both high-velocity hiring and occasional complex or hard-to-fill searches that require deeper, targeted sourcing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management skills and the ability to build trusted partnerships with hiring managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, solutions-oriented approach with strong prioritization and organizational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of structured interviewing, competency-based hiring, and inclusive recruiting practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hourly rate for this role is $60 - $75 per hour. Individual pay decisions are based on a number of factors, including qualifications for the role, experience level, and skillset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role requires active work authorization in the US.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;At Maven we believe that a diverse set of backgrounds and experiences enrich our teams and allow us to achieve above and beyond our goals. If you do not have experience in all of the areas detailed above, we hope that you will share your unique background with us in your application and how it can be additive to our teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits That Work For You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our benefits are designed to support your health, well-being and career development, helping you thrive both personally and professionally. We remain focused on providing a competitive benefits package for our employees. On top of standards such as employer-covered health, dental, and insurance plan options, we offer an inclusive approach to benefits:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maven for Mavens: access to the full platform and specialists, including care for mental health, reproductive health, family planning and pediatrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Whole-self care through wellness partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work, in office meals, and work together days&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;16 weeks 100% paid parental leave and new parent stipend (for Mavens who&#39;ve been with us for 1 year+)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual professional development stipend and access to a personal career coach through Maven for Mavens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K matching for US-based employees, with immediate vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;These benefits are applicable to Maven Clinic Co., US-based, full-time employees only. 1099/Contract Providers are ineligible for these benefits.&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is an affirmativ

&lt;p&gt;eClinical Solutions helps life sciences organizations around the world accelerate clinical development initiatives with expert data services and the elluminate Clinical Data Cloud – the foundation of digital trials. Together, the elluminate platform and digital data services give clients self-service access to all their data from one centralized location plus advanced analytics that help them make smarter, faster business decisions.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;OVERVIEW:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Technical Project Manager is responsible for ensuring the delivery of quality products and services to eCS clients and partners. Most importantly, the Technical Project Managers oversee the successful delivery of eCS’ elluminate® product, a next generation data integration and analytics cloud platform that enables life sciences organizations to optimize the aggregation, standardization, and analysis of their data throughout the clinical development lifecycle. Additionally, they develop roadmaps and timelines for executing the highest quality of technical services and support including but not limited to solution integration, custom reporting, data mapping and Clinical Data Repository (CDR). eCS Project Managers are responsible for developing and maintaining detailed project documentation, managing client expectations and approvals on scoped deliverables, balancing and reconciling the project budget, serving as the point person for project communication and issue escalation, effectively realigning resources in response to scope changes and proactively mitigating other potential risks, fostering positive and long-lasting client relationships, driving elluminate® utilization, and driving project efforts toward successful (on time, on budget, within scope) completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;KEY TASKS &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead and drive elluminate® implementation projects throughout the project lifecycle by consistently using PMI-compliant and eCS-required methodologies, standards and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully manage multiple software implementation projects simultaneously, ensuring that proper documentation is developed and maintained, that project risks are mitigated with a collaborative team approach and that client satisfaction remains at the forefront of all efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal and external subject matter experts to deliver seamless elluminate integration, rapid system adoption and end-user utilization, and the highest quality of professional services to our clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;EDUCATION/ EXPERIENCE:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Science or Master of Science degree in Computer Science and/or equivalent work experience preferred &nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of systems/software project management experience preferably in a clinical, biomedical, or software environment preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clinical data management experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;PROFESSIONAL SKILLS:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional multi-tasking and time management skills, including the ability to effectively resource competing priorities and adapt to changing client demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills and an ability to effectively partner with audiences at all levels of the eCS and client organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to utilizing operational standards, PMI methodologies and best practices with a focus on process efficiencies and revenue growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;TECHNICAL SKILLS&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with Microsoft applications (Word, Outlook, Excel, PowerPoint, Project, Visio, Teams, etc.) and collaborative platforms like MS Teams, OneDrive and SharePoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing client projects that focus on technical deployments, system implementations, and/or data management and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some knowledge of ICH/GCP guidelines, 21 CFR Part 11, clinical trials methodology, CRO partnerships, and EDC systems (Medidata, Rave) is highly desired&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Accelerate your skills and career within a fast-growing company while impacting the future of healthcare. We have shared our story, now we look forward to learning yours!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;eClinical Solutions is a people first organization. Our inclusive culture values the contribution that diversity brings to our business. We celebrate individual experiences that connect us and that inspire innovation in our community. Our team seeks out opportunities to learn, grow and continuously improve. Bring your authentic self, you are welcome here!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer that values diversity. Our management team is committed to the principle that employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, culture fit and business need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Job Summary&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Application Support Engineer II to join our 24x7 Follow the Sun support team. You will be the front line for alert response and resolution, collaborating with cross-functional teams to identify and resolve technical issues, alerts, and cases. Effective communication with customers and stakeholders is essential, as you will need to relay status updates and escalate issues as necessary. The role demands excellent troubleshooting and problem-solving skills. Hybrid work options may be available, offering flexibility while maintaining round-the-clock support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work Customer issues in assigned SalesForce queue by troubleshooting application issues, and closing the loop with all parties involved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the definition and management of application layer technology standards and processes including but not limited to: software version, configuration management, load balancing, database connectivity, and release/maintenance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring tool administration (ProActiveNet, AlertSite, datadog, cloudwatch, PRTG, PagerDuty, graylog, Kibana, custom scripts).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new customer implementations and the transitions from lower environments to production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to technical application questions and issues raised by customers in support of our Operating Level agreements. Handle escalations using a swarming methodology.&nbsp; Available in Hip Chat and Skype rooms during business hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to off hour’s pages and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participates in maintenance, performance testing, operations acceptance testing (OAT) and / or release activities as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer assigned JIRA ticket queues and follow up with appropriate parties. Regularly, clearly and effectively communicate pertinent information to team members, management and customers according to Support service level standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback to product and development teams to improve usability and functionality of GHX applications.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adopt and participate in Knowledge Centered Support (KCS) by creating and modifying articles in SalesForce.&nbsp; Articles should be sufficient to resolve cases and major service disruptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of Application Support or related experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work from own initiative, learn quickly, and function effectively with team members in a high pressure and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must demonstrate effective listening, verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unix or Windows application production/customer support experience. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-focused attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with task automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with environment monitoring tools (Cloudwatch/Datadog/PagerDuty/etc...).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazon Web Services (AWS) or cloud based architecture support experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and work with complex enterprise application environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and ability to follow established procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ITIL or MOF Change Management concepts (desired)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Oracle/SQL Server and RDBMS concepts (desired)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills (must have experience with a subset of the following):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Windows and/or Unix OS proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS – Amazon Web Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, Perl, Unix and/or Windows scripting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JBoss Application Server&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JSON and restful API experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apache Tomcat&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IIS Application Server&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of OSI Model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JVM monitoring tools (jvmstat, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network monitoring (snoop, NetMon)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EDI (ANSI/X12), and XML knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTTPS, AS2, SFTP protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MySQL, MongoDB, DynamoDB, MSSQL, Oracle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education / Certification(s)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-year degree in computer science or related field or equivalent experience (required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;GHX: It&#39;s the way you do business in healthcare&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Global Healthcare Exchange (GHX) enables better patient care and billions in savings for the healthcare community by maximizing automation, efficiency and accuracy of business processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GHX is a healthcare business and data automation company, empowering healthcare organizations to enable better patient care and maximize industry savings using our world class cloud-based supply chain technology exchange platform, solutions, analytics and services. We bring together healthcare providers and manufacturers and distributors in North America and Europe - who rely on smart, secure healthcare-focused technology and comprehensive data to automate their business processes and make more informed decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is our passion and vision for a more operationally efficient healthcare supply chain, helping organizations reduce - not shift - the cost of doing business, paving the way to delivering patient care more effectively. Together we take more than a billion dollars out of the cost of delivering healthcare every year. GHX is privately owned, operates in the United States, Canada and Europe, and employs more than 1000 people worldwide. Our corporate headquarters is in Colorado, with additional offices in Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
