&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maven Clinic is the world&#39;s largest virtual clinic for women and families on a mission to make healthcare work for all of us. Through Maven Enterprise, the company partners with more than 2,300 employers and health plans to provide end-to-end women&#39;s and family health programs spanning fertility and family building, maternity and newborn care, parenting and pediatrics, and menopause and midlife — improving clinical outcomes, reducing healthcare costs, and expanding equitable access to high-quality care at scale. Through its consumer platform, Maven provides direct access to virtual care across 30+ specialties, as well as dedicated hormone and GLP-1 care programs purpose-built for women. Founded in 2014 by CEO Kate Ryder, Maven Clinic has raised more than $425 million from leading healthcare and technology investors including General Catalyst, Sequoia, Dragoneer Investment Group, Oak HC/FT, StepStone Group, Icon Ventures, and Lux Capital. Recognized for innovation and industry leadership, Maven has been named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies, CNBC Disruptor 50, Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative Companies, and FORTUNE Best Places to Work. Learn more at mavenclinic.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An award-winning culture working towards an important mission –&nbsp; Maven Clinic is a recipient of over 30 workplace and innovation awards, including:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TIME 100 Most Influential Companies (2023, 2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Change the World (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC Disruptor 50 List (2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Care Delivery is the infrastructure that powers how Maven members access care and how our providers deliver it. Every program we run across maternity, fertility, menopause, and pediatrics, depends on it. It&#39;s where clinical workflows, provider tooling, and the systems that make care measurable, billable, and scalable at Maven&#39;s scale all come together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Product Manager to help build that platform: the EHR and clinical tooling, provider workflows, messaging, and the data and billing infrastructure that turn Maven&#39;s care model into something reliable and scalable. You&#39;ll own defined capabilities within the platform and drive them from problem to shipped, in close partnership with engineering, clinical, design, and operations. It&#39;s a high-leverage seat. What you build here touches every program Maven offers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to the Group Product Manager, Care Delivery, and work closely with our providers, as well as Clinical Product, Member Experience, Operations, and the Data and AI Platform teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own specific Care Delivery capabilities end-to-end, provider workflows, clinical documentation, messaging, scheduling and matching, or quality and billing infrastructure, from problem definition through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make crisp, well-reasoned product decisions, especially where clinical accuracy and provider experience are both at stake.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI hands-on to move faster, prototyping with AI tools to test ideas and pressure-test flows before committing engineering time, and identify and build AI-powered capabilities into the care delivery platform where they genuinely improve the provider or member experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner daily with engineering and design to ship reliable platform capabilities, and with clinical and operations partners so that what you build works for real providers and members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate regulatory and quality requirements, like HEDIS measures and clinical coding, into clean product experiences that add value without adding friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument what you ship, watch how it performs, and iterate. Bring data to every decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build platform primitives, reusable capabilities that serve many programs, rather than one-off features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a point of view on how AI can improve care delivery workflows, and put it to work in how you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in product management, ideally with some time in healthcare tech or another complex, regulated, or operations-heavy domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong executor: you take ambiguous problems, break them down, and ship, without needing everything defined for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid data instincts: you define the right metrics, work with real datasets, and communicate findings clearly to both clinical and commercial audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with technical and clinical complexity: you can hold your own in an engineering sprint and a clinical review, and you&#39;re eager to learn the domain fast (FHIR, interoperability, EHR workflows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine care for providers and members: the people using what you build show up in your decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct communication and strong cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI and a genuine desire to build with it: you understand how modern AI models work well enough to know where they&#39;re reliable and where they aren&#39;t, you reach for AI tools to prototype and think, and you&#39;re excited to ship AI-powered features rather than just talk about them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience with EHR or EMR systems, clinical workflows, healthcare interoperability, or provider-facing tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is&nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;155,000-185,000 &lt;/strong&gt;per year.&nbsp;You will also be entitled to receive equity and benefits. Individual pay decisions are based on qualifications, experience, and skillset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven embraces a flexible hybrid work model. &lt;strong&gt;This role is open to candidates in remote locations with a strong preference for San Francisco, CA; secondary locations include Seattle, WA and New York, NY.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams primarily operate from the New York Metropolitan area, NY, San Francisco/Bay Area, CA, and Seattle, WA. For those in our New York City office, we encourage in-person collaboration by requiring team members to work onsite three days a week&nbsp; (Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday). For those based in San Francisco/Bay Area

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Service Line Advisor, you will serve as part of the GHX Value Analysis Advisory Services Team, where you will pair your subject-matter expertise with evidence to formulate and deliver actionable recommendations for medical device use in health systems. You will bring, and develop, a comprehensive perspective on cardiovascular, interventional radiology (IR), and general surgery device spend and utilization trends and combine this with GHX Value Analysis&#39;s clinical expertise to advise health system leadership and physicians on opportunities to reduce unwarranted variation and unnecessary device costs and improve patient outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have deep expertise in cardiovascular, interventional radiology, and general surgery device use, strategic sourcing strategy and the US vendor landscape, share a passion for learning and understanding medical device technology, and be excited to use evidence-based solutions to transform healthcare. Additionally, a successful candidate will be a collaborative, energetic problem solver with a successful track record of leading medical device utilization and cost-reduction projects, with a focus on driving both business impact and stakeholder satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the go-to expert in health system Cardiovascular, Interventional Radiology, and General Surgery device sourcing strategy (e.g., cardiac rhythm management, coronary/peripheral interventional devices, embolization and vascular access devices, energy/vessel-sealing devices, surgical mesh, etc.); apply medical device industry expertise to proactively build a knowledge base of market trends, best practice product selection and utilization, vendor landscape, and reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Become a trusted advisor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze and interpret clinical and financial data to inform value-based device spend decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain up-to-date knowledge of GHX Value Analysis&#39;s research, evidence insights and recommendations, as well as market dynamics and device trends across cardiovascular, IR, and general surgery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand client current-state strategic sourcing processes and recommend best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combine quantitative analysis and subject-matter expertise to tailor and present actionable sourcing and utilization strategies for health system leadership (e.g., CMOs, senior physicians, service line leaders, supply chain executives) to reduce costs and improve outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple concurrent client engagements focused on using evidence-based strategies to significantly reduce cost and unwarranted variation in physician preference item (PPI) use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use expertise to engage with supply chain and clinician clients in informed discussions (e.g., scope of work, content deliveries, gathering feedback, current state and recommended best practices)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advance innovation and operational efficiencies internally&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the solution advisory team to build and maintain a scalable, relevant approach to presenting device/service line content that educates clients on evidence, device comparisons, and strategy recommendations, and align approach internally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring perspective to shape GHX Value Analysis&#39;s advisory services model by developing high-impact processes and reusable, scalable tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate and update internal stakeholders (leadership and relevant business units) on the latest device trends (spend and utilization) and healthcare sourcing strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support GHX Value Analysis&#39;s broader product development and research prioritization by providing thought leadership and communicating feedback from clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As needed, serve as a liaison to GHX Value Analysis&#39;s sales and marketing teams to represent our clients&#39; needs and the value GHX Value Analysis delivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in business or healthcare administration, supply chain, or a clinical-related field (or equivalent work- or education-related experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years&#39; experience at a healthcare provider, medical device manufacturer, or healthcare consultancy with deep focus in cardiovascular, interventional radiology, and/or general surgery devices (e.g., cardiac rhythm management, coronary/peripheral interventional devices, embolization and vascular access devices, energy/vessel-sealing devices, surgical mesh, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of device sourcing strategies and vendor/device utilization and standardization initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience analyzing and interpreting clinical and financial healthcare data to derive actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obsessed about impact -- ability to quickly identify underlying drivers of problems, develop hypotheses, and execute on a path to solve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and ability to effectively influence and communicate complicated ideas and present to senior leaders in a health system, especially physician and other clinical leadership, with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer service focus; ability to demonstrate good judgment, tact, and diplomacy in dealing with internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent project management skills, including attention to detail, ability to independently prioritize work, and ability to collaborate across multiple teams while managing multiple projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced environment, adapts quickly, and successfully manages ambiguity; doer mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Excel and PowerPoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to client sites as necessary (approximately 20% travel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation range:&lt;/strong&gt; $105,000 - $115,000.&lt;br&gt;The base salary range represents the anticipated low and high end of the GHX’s salary range for this position. Actual salaries will vary and will be based on various factors, such as the candidate’s qualifications, skills, competencies, and proficiency for the role. The base salary is one component of GHX’s total compensation package for employees. Other rewards and benefits include health, vision, and dental insurance, accident and life insurance, 401k matching, paid-time off, and education reimbursement, to name a few. To view more details of our benefits, visit us here: https://www.ghx.com/about/careers/&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
