&lt;p&gt;Truveta is the world&#39;s first health provider led data platform with a vision of Saving Lives with Data. Our mission is to enable researchers to find cures faster, empower every clinician to be an expert, and help families make the most informed decisions about their care. Achieving Truveta&#39;s ambitious vision requires an incredible team of talented and inspired people with a special combination of health, software, and big data experience who share our company values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in the greater Seattle area, with our office located in Hyderabad, India.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who We Need&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Truveta is rapidly building a talented and diverse team to tackle complex health and technical challenges. Beyond core capabilities, we are seeking problem solvers, passionate and collaborative teammates, and those willing to roll up their sleeves while making a difference. If you are interested in the opportunity to pursue purposeful work, join a mission-driven team, and build a rewarding career while having fun, Truveta may be the perfect fit for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;This Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Patients, doctors, and medical researchers deserve to benefit from the same large-scale technological innovation and digital intelligence that have driven progress in office productivity, entertainment, and social networking. We are looking for a Full Stack Senior Software Engineer excited by the opportunity to improve health care in far-reaching ways. In this role, you will lead and build modern, scalable software solutions across the full stack to streamline our engineering processes and accelerate our mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate with internal users to analyze their use cases, requirements, and expectations, and lead the design and development of scalable, secure, and cost-effective cloud-based software solutions that remove inefficiencies and pain points, enabling our users to deliver faster and do more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role also gives you the opportunity to work closely with other senior and principal software engineers across the company to help define our software future direction and long-term strategy, and to influence technology selection in ways that make a significant impact on our business success. You will also mentor and guide junior software engineers, helping to improve their code quality and security practices and supporting their growth by championing SDLC best practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We Are Seeking a Full Stack Senior Software Engineer Who:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has 7 plus years of strong expertise and hands-on experience in coding, testing, source control, CI/CD pipelines, and APIs in the cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has proven experience building reliable, secure, and scalable software solutions using modern cloud-based paradigms, across both front-end and back-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a quick learner who knows how to iterate and evolve a software solution while carefully balancing the needs of privacy, security, and reliability against a changing product landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides consultation and subject matter expertise for software development, rollout, and maintenance through the full software lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads major projects and program initiatives, participates in sprint planning, removes roadblocks, and ensures on-time delivery with quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is willing to review code developed by other software engineers and provide feedback to ensure best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is willing to commit to ongoing training on key topics such as privacy, compliance, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is willing to join an on-call rotation to triage production software issues and recover services quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science or a related technical discipline, or equivalent years of experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated working knowledge translating a business requirement into a functional design, development, testing, and implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of coding experience building production-quality software in a team setting is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience building full stack cloud applications with technologies such as Python, .NET, Node.js, React, or Java is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with serverless RESTful APIs to support API-driven services for system-to-system usage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with modern cloud-native platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience with DevOps tools such as Git and CI/CD pipelines; Azure DevOps experience is a big plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work with the Azure platform, including Azure Functions/Web Apps and Azure Storage accounts, is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work with Azure Kubernetes Service and containerized application development is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Azure security services such as Azure Networking, Azure Firewall, and Azure Key Vault is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with testing frameworks for React, Node.js, and C#/.NET.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Truveta?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be a part of building something special. Now is the perfect time to join Truveta. We have strong, established leadership with decades of success. We are well-funded. We are building a culture that prioritizes people and their passions across personal, professional, and everything in between. Join us as we build an amazing company together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Truveta is committed to creating a diverse, inclusive, and empowering workplace. We believe that having employees with diverse backgrounds enables Truveta to better meet our mission and serve patients and health communities around the world.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;eClinical Solutions is a global leader in clinical data intelligence, delivering the elluminate® Clinical Data Cloud® — an AI-powered platform driving agentic data review, SDTM automation, and RBQM for 18 of the top 50 pharmaceutical companies worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our eNOVA AI-First transformation, we are embedding AI across every pillar of clinical development and enterprise operations — compressing cycle times, improving data quality, and redefining how work gets done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we scale our AI capabilities, we are building a high-impact, hands-on AI engineering function focused on delivering real, production-grade automation across the enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will make an impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Principal AI Engineer – Automation &amp; AI is a hands-on technical leader responsible for designing, building, and deploying AI-powered automation solutions across eClinical Solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is builder-first (70–80% hands-on development) and operates within a small, high-output team (2–4 engineers). You will work directly with the CTAO and business leaders to identify high-value use cases and rapidly translate them into working AI systems in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a program management or oversight role. You are expected to build, ship, and iterate continuously, leveraging modern AI tooling and agentic frameworks to deliver measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Accelerate your skills and career within a fast-growing company while impacting the future of healthcare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your day to day:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building &amp; Shipping AI Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy agentic AI workflows and automation solutions across enterprise functions including R&amp;D, Engineering, Professional Services, IT, Finance, Sales, and Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build production-grade systems such as:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-agent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RAG-based applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document intelligence and summarization pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow and process automation solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use modern AI tools and frameworks including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Codex, Claude Code, Gemini, NotebookLM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex (or equivalents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly prototype, validate, and deploy solutions in weeks, not months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owning End-to-End Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business problems into working AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design lightweight architectures and iterate quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prompt engineering strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestration logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API integrations and data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing, validation, and monitoring frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with stakeholders to refine outputs and drive adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving High-Velocity Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver continuous output with weekly or bi-weekly releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize use cases based on:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ROI and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical feasibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speed to value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with minimal process and high accountability in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contributing to Scalable AI Foundations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reusable assets including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prompt templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agent design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration utilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to lightweight standards for:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security and data handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible AI practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluation and performance monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership &amp; Mentorship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance to a small team of AI engineers and automation specialists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example through hands-on contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the evolution of the AI engineering function as it scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take the first step towards your dream career. Here is what we are looking for in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10+ years of software engineering experience with recent hands-on work in AI/LLM systems&lt;/li&gt;
