&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RAG architectures and vector databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI evaluation frameworks, guardrails, and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workflow automation tools and enterprise integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated environments (e.g., life sciences, healthcare, financial services)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with clinical data, CDISC standards, or clinical development workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-growth or PE-backed SaaS environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Use Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees are expected to appropriately leverage company-approved AI tools to improve productivity and quality while adhering to company policies, protecting confidential information, validating AI-generated content, and exercising sound professional judgment. AI is intended to augment—not replace—professional judgment, critical thinking, accountability, and decision-making.&nbsp;Acc

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maven Clinic is the world&#39;s largest virtual clinic for women and families on a mission to make healthcare work for all of us. Through Maven Enterprise, the company partners with more than 2,300 employers and health plans to provide end-to-end women&#39;s and family health programs spanning fertility and family building, maternity and newborn care, parenting and pediatrics, and menopause and midlife — improving clinical outcomes, reducing healthcare costs, and expanding equitable access to high-quality care at scale. Through its consumer platform, Maven provides direct access to virtual care across 30+ specialties, as well as dedicated hormone and GLP-1 care programs purpose-built for women. Founded in 2014 by CEO Kate Ryder, Maven Clinic has raised more than $425 million from leading healthcare and technology investors including General Catalyst, Sequoia, Dragoneer Investment Group, Oak HC/FT, StepStone Group, Icon Ventures, and Lux Capital. Recognized for innovation and industry leadership, Maven has been named to the TIME100 Most Influential Companies, CNBC Disruptor 50, Fast Company&#39;s Most Innovative Companies, and FORTUNE Best Places to Work. Learn more at mavenclinic.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An award-winning culture working towards an important mission –&nbsp; Maven Clinic is a recipient of over 30 workplace and innovation awards, including:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TIME 100 Most Influential Companies (2023, 2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Change the World (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CNBC Disruptor 50 List (2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a strategic narrative leader to own and evolve Maven&#39;s go-to-market narrative. This role owns how Maven explains itself — to the employers and health plans evaluating our platform and care management programs, to clients demonstrating the quantitative and qualitative value of Maven, and to members navigating some of life&#39;s most important healthcare decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role. You&#39;ll define and maintain the narrative frameworks that anchor everything we take to market: the pitch deck, the positioning, the campaign themes, the launch moments. This is a role for someone who operates at the intersection of strategist and writer — you&#39;re equally comfortable defining the framework and doing the writing yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person is wired for both strategy and execution. You&#39;ve worked at the intersection of consulting-style systems thinking and editorial-quality writing. You move fluidly between strategic framework-building and high-quality written execution. You use AI fluently — it&#39;s woven into how you research, think, and write.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report into the Director of GTM Narrative within the Growth organization, working closely with Product Marketing, Communications, Clinical, and executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve Maven&#39;s core narrative, ensuring one coherent story that connects employer value and member experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the overarching narrative for major company moments (e.g., new product launches, strategic partnerships, and other defining company moments)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own narrative for existing clients across key moments to drive stakeholder engagement and partnership expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the primary corporate pitch deck and keep it current with product strategy, clinical evidence, and competitive positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing to ensure product positioning lives within a company narrative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate clinical research, outcomes data, and product capabilities into credible stories that resonate with executive buyers and clients alike&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a living narrative system: messaging hierarchy, core value propositions, and usage guidelines for cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build feedback loops with Growth and field teams to understand what&#39;s actually landing in buyer and member conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You May Be a Good Fit If You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6-8+ years of experience shaping narrative or messaging at a high-growth technology, healthcare, or consumer-facing company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have operated at the intersection of B2B and consumer audiences, ideally in healthcare, healthtech, or another regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are oriented to the close. You&#39;ve built positioning designed to win deals. You understand narrative as a commercial instrument that can transform growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an exceptional writer who can articulate financial impact to executive stakeholders while expressing clinical rigor and empathy to members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think in systems. You build narrative infrastructure, not just one-off deliverables. You&#39;re comfortable working from data — outcomes studies, utilization rates, financial impact — and know how to turn numbers into a coherent argument, not just a stat in a slide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and emerging technologies to accelerate research, refine ideas, and scale narrative development without compromising rigor or clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence cross-functional partners through clarity, credibility, and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn fast and visibly. This role sits at the intersection of healthcare, business, and clinical evidence — you don&#39;t need to know all three on day one, but you need to come in curious and get up to speed quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Candidates May Also Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in management consulting combined with in-house operating experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with go-to-market narrative done at deal speed — turning positioning, packaging, and pricing into language that closes deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthtech or another regulated industry where rigor and accessibility have to coexist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with messaging work that moved real outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a function or practice from scratch, not inheriting a mature team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $150,000 - $180,000 per year. You will also be entitled to receive equity and b

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you looking for a role in a company that&#39;s solving one of the greatest challenges of our lifetime?&nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Ophelia helps people end their opioid use and restore their quality of life with respect for their time and dignity. Our mission is to make evidence-based treatments for opioid use disorder (OUD) accessible to everyone... and we&#39;re looking to bring more people onto our team to help us achieve it.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://ophelia.com/&quot;&gt;Ophelia&lt;/a&gt; is a venture-backed, healthcare startup that helps individuals with OUD by providing FDA-approved medication and clinical care through a telehealth platform. Our approach is discreet, convenient, and affordable. We&#39;ve been successfully operating in 16 states for almost six years and we&#39;re excited to continue our growth. We are a team of physicians, scientists, entrepreneurs, researchers and White House advisors, backed by leading technology and healthcare investors working to re-imagine and re-build OUD treatment in America.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ophelia is seeking a part-time Technical Recruiter to lead hiring across our technology departments, including Software Engineering, Data, Product Management, and Product Design. This role is ideal for someone who thrives on sourcing incredible technical talent, building genuine relationships with candidates, and partnering closely with hiring managers to make amazing hires. It is a full-cycle recruiting role, including research, sourcing, interview coordination, candidate management, and closing. A successful Tech Recruiter at Ophelia is someone who is proactive, goal-oriented, and genuinely motivated by helping candidates find their dream in our growing tech teams. We’re looking for someone who can bring a strong point of view on what excellent technical hiring looks like, while staying flexible enough to adapt it to Ophelia&#39;s fast-paced, mission-driven environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a part-time role at approximately 20 hours/week, reporting to Ophelia&#39;s Talent Acquisition Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Full-Cycle Technical Recruiting:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage sourcing, screening, and closing for open roles across the tech team; this could be software engineering, data/analytics, product, and design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source Creatively:&lt;/strong&gt; Go beyond inbound applicants by building and running proactive sourcing strategies to find passive, high-caliber technical talent; can easily manage complex or niche searches with narrow or highly specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Nurture Campaigns:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and maintain talent pipelines and nurture campaigns so we have warm relationships with strong candidates before roles open.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver a Great Candidate Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure every technical candidate has a transparent, respectful, and well-paced experience with Ophelia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design &amp; Refine Interview Plans:&lt;/strong&gt; Build effective, role-specific interview plans in partnership with hiring managers, and adjust them based on what&#39;s working, and what isn’t.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Hiring Managers:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a trusted advisor to tech leadership, helping calibrate role requirements and interview processes, pressure-test job descriptions, and keep pipelines moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use Data to Drive Decisions:&lt;/strong&gt; Track pipeline health and hiring metrics, and use those insights to identify bottlenecks and adjust sourcing or process in real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn the Business:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop a working understanding of Ophelia&#39;s way of working, and our tech team’s hiring preferences, so you can align your recruiting approach accordingly.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the Details in Greenhouse:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep requisitions, candidate stages, and reporting clean and current.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp; Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years of technical recruiting experience&lt;/strong&gt;, in in-house or corporate recruiting roles.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Well-networked&lt;/strong&gt;; has dedicated time throughout their career building a fantastic network of technical talent that they can lean on in this role.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated success sourcing for complex technical roles in high demand&lt;/strong&gt;, including software engineering, data/analytics, product, and/or design roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Intrinsically motivated by service to hiring teams&lt;/strong&gt; as you find real satisfaction in helping others hire well, not just in closing reqs.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative by default; &lt;/strong&gt;our Tech Team is rooted in an agile approach, centered on continuous alignment, growth, and learning.&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly organized,&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to juggle multiple searches and stakeholders without dropping details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable working with data and pipeline metrics&lt;/strong&gt; to inform sourcing strategy and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of building candidate nurture campaigns and pipelines&lt;/strong&gt;, not just filling immediate reqs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skilled at designing interview plans and iterating on them&lt;/strong&gt; based on real hiring data and feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity, change, and a fast-paced, evolving environment&lt;/strong&gt;; able to prioritize independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred:&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Greenhouse ATS experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup recruiting experience&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare recruiting experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ophelia Compensation Overview &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We set compensation based on the level and skills required for the role. We value pay transparency and equity, and are committed to fair pay. In order to prevent pay disparities and reduce time spent in negotiations, we take a “first and best” offer approach: this means we’re not holding any compe

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you looking for a role in a company that&#39;s solving one of the greatest challenges of our lifetime?&nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Ophelia helps people end their opioid use and restore their quality of life with respect for their time and dignity. Our mission is to make evidence-based treatments for opioid use disorder (OUD) accessible to everyone... and we&#39;re looking to bring more people onto our team to help us achieve it.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://ophelia.com/&quot;&gt;Ophelia&lt;/a&gt; is a venture-backed, healthcare startup that helps individuals with OUD by providing FDA-approved medication and clinical care through a telehealth platform. Our approach is discreet, convenient, and affordable. We&#39;ve been successfully operating in 16 states for almost six years and we&#39;re excited to continue our growth. We are a team of physicians, scientists, entrepreneurs, researchers and White House advisors, backed by leading technology and healthcare investors working to re-imagine and re-build OUD treatment in America.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About the Role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Analyst, you will turn data into decisions that prove telehealth to be the best way to treat opioid use disorder! You will be the go-to analytical partner for all three of our product squads, shaping how we measure success, designing and reading out experiments, and helping our teams understand what patients truly need. You will work cross-functionally with product managers, engineers, product designers, clinicians, operators, marketers, billers, and more (this role is perfect if you want to fully immerse in technology-enabled healthcare services). You are right for this role if your statistics tools are razor-sharp and you enjoy&nbsp; immersing yourself in experiment construction and analyses. Together, you will frame the right questions, test ideas quickly, and learn in an iterative way. Ultimately, you will make sure our product decisions are grounded in rigorous evidence, centered on patients, and connected to Ophelia&#39;s goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To date, we have built a portfolio of bespoke patient and clinical applications, bespoke billing and clinical data services, and commercial integrations, all of which have been core to achieving our goals. Looking forward, our technology roadmap is rich with innovative opportunities across paid-digital, B2B, and peer-led growth, new clinical services, applications of AI for clinicians and Care Coordinators, and a whole lot more. Every one of these bets needs strong measurement and smart experiments, and that is where you come in. Together, we will build awesome products while we embark towards profitability, our next milestone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Technology team today is small but mighty and works in close collaboration across software engineering, product design, product management, and data. We use an agile approach rooted in the principles of the Agile Manifesto and are growing a strong experiment culture across our squads. Our product suite includes a custom-built EMR platform for our clinical organization and a patient portal, alongside numerous interaction modes (including text messaging, video conferencing, and third-party software). Our analytics stack includes BigQuery, Lightdash, FullStory, and LaunchDarkly, and we work in SQL, Python, and R.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this fully remote role, you will report to Becca Getto, our Manager of Product Management, and support all three of our product squads, working across Technology broadly. You will also partner closely with our Data team through our Data Council, including our Data Analysts and Analytics Engineers. Together, we&#39;ll help hard-to-reach people treat their opioid dependence. You may not have experience in this treatment area, but ideally, you&#39;ll have knowledge of the healthcare space, including understanding health outcomes and benchmarks, systems, and regulatory compliance (HIPAA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead experimentation&lt;/strong&gt; across our product squads, partnering with product managers, engineering, and product design to shape hypotheses, size and design tests, monitor them in flight, and deliver clear readouts. Help grow a culture where every team loves to test and learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design and maintain our product metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, including success metrics, guardrails, and leading indicators for each squad. Validate metric health, build trusted dashboards in Lightdash, and make sure teams can track what matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver deep-dive analyses&lt;/strong&gt; on patient and clinician behavior, including funnels, engagement, retention, and outcomes. When a randomized test isn&#39;t possible, use quasi-experimental methods to get to the best available answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Study and share outcomes&lt;/strong&gt; and learnings with squad teams, our leadership team, and in large format meetings. Turn complex analyses into clear stories and recommendations that drive action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure a patient-centered focus&lt;/strong&gt; by pairing quantitative analysis with qualitative signals such as FullStory sessions, user research, and feedback, so the numbers always connect back to real people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with the Data Council&lt;/strong&gt; and our Data Analysts and Analytics Engineers to improve instrumentation, data quality, shared definitions, and analytics tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay current&lt;/strong&gt; with industry trends, emerging methods, and best practices in product analytics and experimentation. Network frequently beyond Ophelia and share learnings with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Skills &amp; Competencies&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years experience in product analytics&lt;/strong&gt; for consumer-oriented digital products, with a track record of driving stellar business outcomes through experimentation and insight. Demonstrate strong business acumen to connect analyses to strategy, keep track of key metrics and KPIs, and help teams prioritize the work that matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent statistics&lt;/strong&gt; with deep, hands-on command of experimentation methods, including sample size and power calculations (MDE), variance reduction (e.g., CUPED), sequential and Bayesian approaches, and correcting for common pitfalls such as sample ratio mismatch, novelty effects, and multiple testing. Comfortable choosing the right parametric or non-parametric test, working with ratio metrics, and applying causal inference methods such as diff-in-diff, propensity score matching, reg

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you looking for a role in a company that&#39;s solving one of the greatest challenges of our lifetime?&nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Ophelia helps people end their opioid use and restore their quality of life with respect for their time and dignity. Our mission is to make evidence-based treatments for opioid use disorder (OUD) accessible to everyone... and we&#39;re looking to bring more people onto our team to help us achieve it.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://ophelia.com/&quot;&gt;Ophelia&lt;/a&gt; is a venture-backed, healthcare startup that helps individuals with OUD by providing FDA-approved medication and clinical care through a telehealth platform. Our approach is discreet, convenient, and affordable. We&#39;ve been successfully operating in 16 states for almost six years and we&#39;re excited to continue our growth. We are a team of physicians, scientists, entrepreneurs, researchers and White House advisors, backed by leading technology and healthcare investors working to re-imagine and re-build OUD treatment in America.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clinicians are a critical part of our care team at Ophelia. As an Advanced Practice Practitioner, you will provide clinical care to patients receiving medication for opioid use disorder and a narrow suite of mental health conditions (depression, anxiety, insomnia, etc…).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely alongside other clinicians, triage nurses, and administrative care coordinators to deliver compassionate, evidence-based treatment to patients with OUD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Clinicians offer compassionate, non-stigmatizing support for patients, act as a liaison and advocate for them, and ensure patients receive appropriate care as their needs evolve. Depending on role type, clinicians conduct Intake visits and/or follow-up visits, and work within a team-based approach model of care to deliver high quality care to our patients. We have multiple different clinical role types depending on your experience with MOUD, and through our team-based model of care we provide a strong support system to ensure that you and our patients feel comfortable and supported.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our patient care hours are Monday - Friday 9-7pm and Saturday and Sunday 9-5pm, with our weekend coverage provided only by our most experienced providers! We will work with you to determine your ideal schedule within these hours.&nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ideal candidate is an APP who:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;3+ years of experience as an APP&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a passion for serving vulnerable populations, and;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Either has previous experience caring for individuals with OUD, or&nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;willing to learn&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;the clinical skills needed to provide MOUD through a telehealth platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is looking for full time work in a fast-paced, innovative start-up that values patient-centered care&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;No experience with MOUD is required for this role: we will teach you what you need to know!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role you will be responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treatment Plans:&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;determine individualized treatment plans for patients; facilitate changes to treatment plans when patients are not improving as expected, either independently or consulting with a more experienced provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioral Interventions:&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;use motivational interviewing, behavioral activation and other behavioral interventions as needed to motivate patients to remain in care and adherent to their treatment plan. Conduct behavioral health / psych evals for the suite of psych services we treat (depression, anxiety, insomnia, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitor/Medication Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&nbsp;systematically track treatment response and monitor patients for changes in clinical symptoms and side effects, treatment adherence, the effectiveness of treatment or complications, and prescribe or queue the appropriate medications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;provide patient education on OUD and MOUD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charting&lt;/strong&gt;: Document all patient encounters in Ophelia’s EHR in a timely and high quality manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training and License Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Board Certified Physician Assistant (PA-C) or Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (Psych NP, PMHNP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Oklahoma DEA/CDS license (schedule 3N, 4, 5)&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully licensed to practice in Oklahoma &lt;em&gt;(additional licenses in NJ, NY, VA, PA, DE, or MD a plus!)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide patient-centered, non-judgmental, non-stigmatizing compassionate care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about working with vulnerable or marginalized populations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with a diverse population of people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient and comfortable working in a remote telehealth environment with technological skillset to work across multiple tech platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about working in an early-stage healthcare startup that is fast-paced and always evolving processes and technology to meet patient and clinician needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work in a team-based approach model of patient care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of differential diagnosis of common substance use disorders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic knowledge of psychopharmacology for opioid use disorder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate ability to collaborate and communicate effectively in a team setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain effective and professional relationships with patients and other members of the care team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of evidence-based psychosocial treatments, counseling techniques, or brief behavioral intervention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits Include&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote work anywhere in the United States&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive medical, vision, and health insurance (many plans are fully covered for the employee!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start with 20 days (4 weeks) of PTO, increasing to 5 weeks after 2 years and 6 weeks after 5 years of tenur

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you looking for a role in a company that&#39;s solving one of the greatest challenges of our lifetime?&nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Ophelia helps people end their opioid use and restore their quality of life with respect for their time and dignity. Our mission is to make evidence-based treatments for opioid use disorder (OUD) accessible to everyone... and we&#39;re looking to bring more people onto our team to help us achieve it.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://ophelia.com/&quot;&gt;Ophelia&lt;/a&gt; is a venture-backed, healthcare startup that helps individuals with OUD by providing FDA-approved medication and clinical care through a telehealth platform. Our approach is discreet, convenient, and affordable. We&#39;ve been successfully operating in 16 states for almost six years and we&#39;re excited to continue our growth. We are a team of physicians, scientists, entrepreneurs, researchers and White House advisors, backed by leading technology and healthcare investors working to re-imagine and re-build OUD treatment in America.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Analyst at Ophelia, you will support the core financial operations of a growing multi-state operation: monthly close, financial reporting, cash and treasury management, internal ROI analysis, and annual planning. You&#39;ll report directly to the FP&amp;A Manager and partner with them closely across each of these areas. Strategic Finance is a small team, but this is a fundamentally cross-functional role - you will regularly be working with Operations, Technology, Marketing, and People team leadership on a variety of project types.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;What your first year will look like:&lt;/em&gt; You&#39;ll take ownership of the parts of close and reporting, build a working understanding of the business through its numbers, and grow into broader ownership of internal ROI analyses to drive company growth.&nbsp;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the recurring components of the monthly close, and work alongside our external accounting partner to hold the close calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft the monthly reporting package, covering total company and state-level P&amp;Ls, variable unit economics, and the leadership financials deck, to drive insight into the health of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain department- and state-level budget versus actual reporting. Work with budget owners across the company to explain variances and raise issues early enough to act on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare external financial deliverables, including board and lender materials&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual planning and re-forecast cycles, partnering with department leads to collect and consolidate expense budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run ad hoc internal ROI analyses in collaboration with business partners to help drive company decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp; Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in FP&amp;A, accounting, or a comparable analytical finance role; with a track record of owning monthly close and reporting cycles. Strong accounting foundation, including accrual concepts and how entries flow through the income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow statement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel and financial modeling skills. You can build a model from scratch, and audit someone else&#39;s, follow the logic, and find the thing that&#39;s wrong with it (if any).&nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stellar communications and stakeholder management with a passion for aligning all participants; able to create strong points of view to achieve Ophelia’s strategy, backed with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare (ideally digital healthcare), multi-state operations, or another regulated environment; or exposure to claims-based revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about our mission to make evidence-based addiction treatment universally accessible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with Netsuite, Claude &amp; Claude for Excel, or a BI tool such as Lightdash is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Benefits Include:&nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive medical, vision, and health insurance (many plans are fully covered for the employee!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start with 20 days (4 weeks) of PTO, increasing to 5 weeks after 2 years and 6 weeks after 5 years of tenure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work From Home Stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k Contribution Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits offered through our benefits provider such as life insurance, short and long term disability, financial wellness, virtual primary care, among others!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ophelia Compensation Overview &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We set compensation based on the level and skills required for the role. We value pay transparency and equity, and are committed to fair pay. In order to prevent pay disparities and reduce time spent in negotiations, we take a “first and best” offer approach: this means we’re not holding any compensation back from our candidates, and you can feel confident that our pay is fair and does not vary based on the strength of someone’s negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation is dynamic at Ophelia: as long as the company performs well and meets our targets, there will be opportunities for increased compensation annually. We’re happy to discuss this approach and our bands if you have questions during the interview process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Compensation Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$125,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Interested in learning more about Ophelia and this role? Apply to work with us!&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Note Before Applying &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
