&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces for Millennials (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces in Health Care (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast Company Most Innovative Companies (2020, 2023)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fortune Best Workplaces NY (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is seeking a Customer Success Director to own a portfolio of our most strategic and complex client partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role reporting directly to the VP of Client Success. You will act as a trusted advisor to VP-level Benefits leaders, own global account strategy, and drive measurable business and clinical outcomes across a portfolio of high-value employer and payer accounts. As the team grows, this role may evolve into a player-coach, taking on direct reports alongside your book. Candidates with people leadership experience are encouraged to raise it, though it is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is both strategic and revenue-driving, taking direct accountability for net revenue retention, renewal health, and expansion readiness. You will translate member outcomes into quantifiable business value for clients, orchestrate cross-functional motions with Sales, Renewals, Product, and Analytics, and build the strategic account plans that protect and grow Maven&#39;s revenue. This is not a reactive support role. It is a commercial leadership position that requires equal parts relationship depth, analytical rigor, and business acumen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates who thrive in this role may have previously held titles such as Client Success Manager, Account Manager, Relationship Manager, Sales Executive, or Account Executive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report directly to the VP of Client Success, partnering closely on account strategy, operating cadence, and Client Success priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own executive-level relationships with VP-level Benefits leaders, brokers, and consultants across a portfolio of high-value accounts, positioning Maven as a strategic partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive enrollment attainment and expansion pipeline across your book, partnering with Renewal Managers on renewals and Sales Directors on expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the playbooks, standards, and operating cadence that make Client Success repeatable and scalable, including account planning, business reviews, escalation paths, and CRM discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively map and engage new stakeholders across complex client organizations, expanding Maven&#39;s influence and identifying new business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate client business goals into actionable success plans that demonstrate how Maven&#39;s solutions drive ROI, cost savings, and measurable business and clinical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling, executive-ready narratives through business reviews and strategic updates tailored for benefits leadership audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence internal teams across Product, Operations, Marketing, and Clinical with client insights to shape roadmap, delivery, and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and elevate Client Success teammates by modeling best-in-class commercia

