&lt;p&gt;Role Summary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an junior or intermediate-level IT Support Engineer to provide general IT support for our global corporate environment. This role will support employees with day-to-day technical issues, Windows/macOS laptop setup, local admin, software access, Microsoft 365 support, Office Wi-Fi, badge and surveillant camera system and basic network troubleshooting, Windows365 Cloud PC support, and IT operational tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate should have basic troubleshooting skills, good customer service mindset, and experience supporting users in a corporate IT environment. This role is suitable for someone who has moved beyond basic helpdesk support and can independently handle common IT issues, escalations, documentation, and operational follow-up.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide &lt;strong&gt;Tier 1/Tier 2 IT support&lt;/strong&gt; for Windows/macOS devices, peripherals, Microsoft 365 applications, browsers, VPN, Wi-Fi, and conference room AV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot hardware, software, operating system, connectivity, and access-related issues for onsite and remote employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support &lt;strong&gt;employee onboarding and offboarding&lt;/strong&gt;, including laptop setup, account/access provisioning, first-day IT support, equipment recovery, and access removal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage user accounts and application access, including password resets, MFA, shared mailboxes, distribution lists, group memberships, and SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain &lt;strong&gt;IT hardware and asset inventory&lt;/strong&gt;, coordinate device shipping, replacements, repairs, warranty claims, and keep asset records up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage IT incidents and service requests through the ticketing system, ensuring timely resolution within SLAs and proper documentation and escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide basic &lt;strong&gt;network and office IT support&lt;/strong&gt;, including Wi-Fi, VPN, conference room systems, and coordination with network/infrastructure teams or vendors when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain IT documentation, including troubleshooting guides, onboarding/offboarding checklists, asset procedures, and knowledge base articles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring issues and recommend improvements to IT support processes and the overall employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 – 3 years of experience in IT support, desktop support, service desk, or IT administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience supporting Windows laptops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic to intermediate macOS support experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft 365: Outlook, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, Office apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting hardware, software, network, and access issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ticketing systems such as ServiceNow, Jira Service Management, Zendesk, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of user accounts, groups, MFA, and basic access management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting remote users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal English communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and follow documented processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer service mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;Experience with Microsoft Intune, Jamf, or other device management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Entra ID / Azure AD basic administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Zoom, Slack, Google Workspace, or other collaboration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic PowerShell scripting knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with asset management tools&lt;/li&gt;
