&lt;p&gt;eClinical Solutions helps life sciences organizations around the world accelerate clinical development initiatives with expert data services and the elluminate Clinical Data Cloud – the foundation of digital trials. Together, the elluminate platform and digital data services give clients self-service access to all their data from one centralized location plus advanced analytics that help them make smarter, faster business decisions.&nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director, Clinical Data Management, is responsible for executing strategic direction and ensuring effective end-to-end data management services across programs and studies. This role has primary leadership responsibility for the&nbsp;India-based CDM organization and is accountable for elevating the quality, consistency, and predictability of clinical&nbsp;data delivery, ensuring that projects meet or exceed established quality standards, timelines, and financial targets. A&nbsp;key focus of the role is to strengthen and mature the Clinical Data Management (CDM) function by enhancing&nbsp;leadership effectiveness, reinforcing core data management fundamentals, and implementing consistent operational&nbsp;oversight and best practices. The Director will also lead the development and scaling of a high-performing team of&nbsp;Clinical Data Management professionals, data analysts, and subject matter experts focused on ongoing data review,&nbsp;proactive data surveillance, and generation of meaningful customer insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In parallel, the Director will play a critical role in modernizing the organization’s data management capabilities&nbsp;through the adoption of risk-based methodologies, advanced analytics, centralized and AI-enabled data review, and&nbsp;other data-driven approaches aligned with broader business objectives. The role partners with internal and external&nbsp;stakeholders optimize data management technologies, processes, and standards while driving cross-functional&nbsp;collaboration to deliver scalable solutions that enhance operational effectiveness and customer value. As a Subject&nbsp;Matter Expert (SME), the Director also contributes to business growth through thought leadership, strategicconsulting, client engagement, and the advancement of differentiated data management and analytics capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY TASKS &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic leadership for the India-based Clinical Data Management (CDM) organization,&nbsp;ensuring high-quality, consistent, and predictable delivery of end-to-end data management services&nbsp;across programs and studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the evolution and maturity of the CDM function by reinforcing data management fundamentals, and implementing standardized operational oversight, governance, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvements, automation initiatives, and adoption of emerging technologies in clinical data management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute initiatives focused on modernizing data review and oversight processes through the use of data insights, analytics, and AI-enabled data review capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a culture of quality, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all CDM activities are executed in compliance with SOPs, ICH/GCP guidelines, regulatory requirements, and applicable quality standards while maintaining inspection readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish, monitor, and report key operational metrics related to quality, productivity, cycle times, delivery predictability, and financial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement continuous improvement initiatives to enhance efficiency and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee resource planning, talent development, organizational capability building, and succession planning to support current delivery needs and future business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with other operational teams to optimize data management processes,&nbsp;standards, systems integration, and delivery models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert (SME) for Clinical Data Management, contributing to innovation initiatives, and development of scalable solutions that enhance customer value and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business development activities through thought leadership, strategic consulting, client presentations, proposal support, and participation in sponsor engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster strong client relationships by promoting a customer-centric culture focused on quality execution, transparency, responsiveness, and long-term partnership growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular operational and strategic updates to executive leadership regarding delivery performance, organizational health, risks, opportunities, and strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties and strategic initiatives as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
